        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Osage County, Oklahoma, Mayes County, Tulsa County, Washington County, Kay County\n- Concepts: county naming, geography, county creation\n\nFacts:\n- Osage County is the largest county in Oklahoma by area.\n- Osage County was created in 1907.\n- Osage County takes its name from the broad rolling hills, rolling tallgrass prairie, and Cross Timbers in the county and nearby areas.\n- The nearby areas referenced in Osage County’s name include parts of Mayes County, Tulsa County, Washington County, and Kay County to the north.",
