        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Osage Hills, Osage County, Oklahoma, Oklahoma, United States\n- Organizations: Osage Nation\n- Topics: geography, county formation, naming\n\nFacts:\n- In 1907, Osage County was created when Oklahoma was admitted as a state.\n- Osage County is named for and is home to the federally recognized Osage Nation.\n- Osage County is the largest county by area in the state of Oklahoma in the United States.\n- The Osage Hills is a hilly area in Oklahoma that is commonly known as \"The Osage.\"\n- The name Osage Hills refers to the broad rolling hills, rolling tallgrass prairie, and Cross Timbers in Osage County and surrounding areas, including parts of Mayes, Tulsa, Washington, and Kay Counties.",
